  "word_method": "independent word generation, not extracted from sentence audio",
  "sentences": [
    {
      "id": 1,
      "text": "Governments around the world are investing capital to push for an end to plastic straws and bags.",
      "file": "assets/audio/sentences/sentence-01.mp3",
      "exists": true
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Businesses are turning to paper products as a choice.",
      "file": "assets/audio/sentences/sentence-02.mp3",
      "exists": true
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Paper is considered by many to be better than plastic.",
      "file": "assets/audio/sentences/sentence-03.mp3",
      "exists": true
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "However, it is harmful to the environment, too.",
      "file": "assets/audio/sentences/sentence-04.mp3",
      "exists": true
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Customers are becoming aware of its negative effects.",
      "file": "assets/audio/sentences/sentence-05.mp3",
      "exists": true
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "Firstly, paper products are made from trees.",
      "file": "assets/audio/sentences/sentence-06.mp3",
      "exists": true
    },
    {
      "id": 7,
      "text": "Trees can reduce carbon dioxide levels in the atmosphere, which slows down climate change.",
      "file": "assets/audio/sentences/sentence-07.mp3",
      "exists": true
    },
    {
      "id": 8,
      "text": "An increase in the use of paper bags is responsible for more acts of cutting down trees.",
      "file": "assets/audio/sentences/sentence-08.mp3",
      "exists": true
    },
    {
      "id": 9,
      "text": "Secondly, paper products require more energy and water.",
      "file": "assets/audio/sentences/sentence-09.mp3",
      "exists": true
    },
    {
      "id": 10,
      "text": "Saving energy and water by recycling seems to be a good idea.",
      "file": "assets/audio/sentences/sentence-10.mp3",
      "exists": true
    },
    {
      "id": 11,
      "text": "However, the recycling process takes even more energy and water than to make a brand new paper bag.",
      "file": "assets/audio/sentences/sentence-11.mp3",
      "exists": true
    },
    {
      "id": 12,
      "text": "So cooperating with recycling programmes will not always be an effective solution.",
      "file": "assets/audio/sentences/sentence-12.mp3",
      "exists": true
    },
    {
      "id": 13,
      "text": "Thirdly, paper products are heavier than plastic ones, so they require more oil to transport.",
      "file": "assets/audio/sentences/sentence-13.mp3",
      "exists": true
    },
    {
      "id": 14,
      "text": "Seven trucks are needed to transport two million paper bags, while only one truck is needed to transport the same number of plastic bags.",
      "file": "assets/audio/sentences/sentence-14.mp3",
      "exists": true
    },
    {
      "id": 15,
      "text": "So the price of transporting paper products can be expensive.",
      "file": "assets/audio/sentences/sentence-15.mp3",
      "exists": true
    },
    {
      "id": 16,
      "text": "The increased weight also leads to a large amount of waste once the bags are thrown away.",
      "file": "assets/audio/sentences/sentence-16.mp3",
      "exists": true
    },
    {
      "id": 17,
      "text": "The most environment-friendly solution is to avoid single-use products altogether.",
      "file": "assets/audio/sentences/sentence-17.mp3",
      "exists": true
    },
    {
      "id": 18,
      "text": "Anyone can contribute by using products like glass water bottles and steel straws.",
      "file": "assets/audio/sentences/sentence-18.mp3",
      "exists": true
    },
    {
      "id": 19,
      "text": "They are convenient and can be used over and over again.",
      "file": "assets/audio/sentences/sentence-19.mp3",
      "exists": true
    }
  ],
